      "writtenOn": "2019-05-09T01:32:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we assume there was no existing contract, we don\u0027t apply Rp, and we discover the source as usual.\n\n- If there actually was, we would HardRst which should cause SrcCaps to be sent again.\n- if there was no contract, we would either respond to a SrcCap or HardRst if we didn\u0027t receive one in time.\n\nIn my opinion, if we fail to read the flags, it\u0027s safer to assume that there was a contract and skip applying the Rp\u0027s. Daisuke\u0027s proposal makes that clearer.",
      "parentUuid": "5f9b9358_bd6a6e27",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2349,
        "startChar": 1,
